1
00:00:24,515 --> 00:00:48,211
[SPEAKER_03]: So, if I think about past memories when I was five, ten, twenty, thirty, to my present experience, there's a sense of continuity or self to whom those experiences happened, which also informs thoughts about the future.

2
00:00:49,481 --> 00:01:00,526
[SPEAKER_03]: So, I was wondering, could that sense of continuity be one way to describe what bhāva is?

3
00:01:01,326 --> 00:01:03,227
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, certainly.

4
00:01:03,447 --> 00:01:06,428
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a form of... well, it's the way you exist.

5
00:01:08,509 --> 00:01:14,692
[SPEAKER_01]: So, Bhakti, that continuity from your past,

6
00:01:16,005 --> 00:01:17,446
[SPEAKER_00]: That you can recollect now.

7
00:01:18,386 --> 00:01:19,967
[SPEAKER_01]: Where is that continuity perceived?

8
00:01:23,008 --> 00:01:23,249
[SPEAKER_00]: Now.

9
00:01:23,729 --> 00:01:24,129
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

10
00:01:24,249 --> 00:01:25,089
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

11
00:01:25,149 --> 00:01:30,072
[SPEAKER_01]: Colors the past with the same owner, but it's actually here and now.

12
00:01:32,316 --> 00:01:42,520
[SPEAKER_01]: And back when that, you know, ten years ago, when that was here and now, that's where that good sense of continuity, sense of I am, that persists throughout these different experiences, that's where it was.

13
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:43,841
[SPEAKER_01]: It was here and now.

14
00:01:43,981 --> 00:01:44,861
[SPEAKER_01]: It's always here and now.

15
00:01:45,561 --> 00:01:47,082
[SPEAKER_01]: That's where that sense of continuity is.

16
00:01:48,142 --> 00:01:49,763
[SPEAKER_01]: That sense of I am, sense of self.

17
00:01:51,644 --> 00:01:54,605
[SPEAKER_03]: So the Buddha wasn't advocating to deny

18
00:01:56,022 --> 00:02:01,326
[SPEAKER_03]: This sense of continuity that he was more seeing... No, sense of continuity is real as such.

19
00:02:01,346 --> 00:02:04,989
[SPEAKER_01]: The mistake, though, is the mistake of ownership.

20
00:02:05,109 --> 00:02:12,874
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the mistake that's, again, perpetuated on the basis of a mind that's not free from greed, aversion, delusion, here and now.

21
00:02:13,655 --> 00:02:23,002
[SPEAKER_01]: So that's why a person who would have uprooted the ownership, freed the mind from conceiving, from the notion of I am, fully developed anatta,

22
00:02:24,302 --> 00:02:28,525
[SPEAKER_01]: As the Buddha says in the suttas, that person would not think, oh, but I was in the past.

23
00:02:28,825 --> 00:02:33,828
[SPEAKER_01]: Now I'm not, because I'm an arahant, but I was in the past and I... or I would be in the future.

24
00:02:33,848 --> 00:02:33,968
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

25
00:02:34,348 --> 00:02:41,572
[SPEAKER_01]: Past and future were equally affected by that same present that has been purified.

26
00:02:41,592 --> 00:02:46,835
[SPEAKER_03]: So, he's fully seeing the sense of continuity as contained within that which is discontinuous.

27
00:02:47,288 --> 00:02:48,149
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah.

28
00:02:48,229 --> 00:03:00,398
[SPEAKER_01]: You see, it's fully unownable, fully dependent on the existence and operation of the five aggregates, on their presence.

29
00:03:01,879 --> 00:03:02,800
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

30
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:08,444
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no... because that's the trick with that sense of continuity and the sense of I am, sense of self.

31
00:03:08,984 --> 00:03:16,090
[SPEAKER_01]: It feels like it's outside of the experience as a whole, as a perpetual entity, owner,

32
00:03:16,813 --> 00:03:22,816
[SPEAKER_01]: To whom these things occur, feelings, perceptions, past, future, but it exists independent of them.

33
00:03:23,636 --> 00:03:31,620
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's changing that order through right contemplation that can only arise on the basis of virtue and sense restraint.

34
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:35,322
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's when then you start to reverse, you start seeing.

35
00:03:35,762 --> 00:03:36,763
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you're not denying.

36
00:03:37,482 --> 00:03:52,227
[SPEAKER_01]: You're not denying the sense of I am, you're not denying the sense of that continuous sense of self that you remember since you were a child, but you're just including it within the arisen, presently arisen feeling, presently arisen perception, intention, state of mind.

37
00:03:52,607 --> 00:03:54,448
[SPEAKER_01]: So, basically, you're putting it second.

38
00:03:54,548 --> 00:03:59,570
[SPEAKER_01]: You're enclosing it where it should be enclosed, so that that gratuitous sense of

39
00:04:02,237 --> 00:04:07,238
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, this is something outside, independent of these feelings that come and go, perceptions come and go.

40
00:04:07,678 --> 00:04:10,179
[SPEAKER_01]: That will fade away.

41
00:04:10,219 --> 00:04:19,301
[SPEAKER_01]: See, people, people have the view and the assumption that their sense of self is independent of the experience as a whole, because that's... they're cultivating it through their attitude and through their action.

42
00:04:20,401 --> 00:04:26,463
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you stop cultivating, you stop providing fuel for it, it will fade away, because it's not actually on the outside.

43
00:04:26,583 --> 00:04:27,923
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not actually independent.

44
00:04:30,435 --> 00:04:35,139
[SPEAKER_03]: And Venerable Aniga brought up a sutta relating to this.

45
00:04:35,339 --> 00:04:38,861
[SPEAKER_03]: I was wondering if I could... Go on, yes.

46
00:04:38,881 --> 00:04:42,204
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, sort of interrogate my interpretation of... yeah.

47
00:04:43,204 --> 00:04:45,966
[SPEAKER_03]: So, it's Majjhima Naikāya 74.

48
00:04:49,339 --> 00:04:50,900
[SPEAKER_03]: There are three kinds of feeling.

49
00:04:51,321 --> 00:04:54,564
[SPEAKER_03]: Pleasant feeling, painful feeling and neutral feeling.

50
00:04:55,204 --> 00:05:00,529
[SPEAKER_03]: On the occasion when one feels pleasant feeling, one does not feel painful or neutral feeling.

51
00:05:01,370 --> 00:05:04,292
[SPEAKER_03]: On that occasion, one feels only pleasant feeling.

52
00:05:05,934 --> 00:05:11,759
[SPEAKER_03]: On the occasion when one feels painful feeling, one does not feel pleasant or neutral feeling.

53
00:05:11,999 --> 00:05:14,701
[SPEAKER_03]: On that occasion, one feels only painful feeling.

54
00:05:15,903 --> 00:05:20,424
[SPEAKER_03]: On the occasion when one feels neutral feeling, one does not feel pleasant or painful feeling.

55
00:05:20,664 --> 00:05:25,925
[SPEAKER_03]: On that occasion, one feels only neutral feeling.

56
00:05:25,945 --> 00:05:32,226
[SPEAKER_03]: So, yeah, so my interpretation is that, basically, it's highlighting... What comes first.

57
00:05:32,606 --> 00:05:33,487
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, exactly.

58
00:05:33,507 --> 00:05:38,227
[SPEAKER_03]: The discontinuity of feeling as a container for your experience as a whole.

59
00:05:38,267 --> 00:05:45,389
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, see, but... by regarding currently enduring feeling as that which is first,

60
00:05:46,535 --> 00:05:51,221
[SPEAKER_01]: Means that's the entirety of your container, of your present experience.

61
00:05:51,821 --> 00:06:03,095
[SPEAKER_01]: So, whether you are now having... remembering something from your past, planning for the future, that is done within the current enduring feeling.

62
00:06:04,557 --> 00:06:09,058
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just that people's attitude towards their own feelings and perceptions, as I said, they put them second.

63
00:06:09,858 --> 00:06:25,161
[SPEAKER_01]: So, they don't recognize that... not just that there is a pleasant... like, if there is a pleasant feeling currently present, that's the only feeling you feel, as the Sutta says, but that's really... your entire existence is within that current feeling that endures.

64
00:06:25,701 --> 00:06:27,902
[SPEAKER_01]: And when the new feeling comes up, so to speak,

65
00:06:28,719 --> 00:06:38,922
[SPEAKER_01]: When this feeling ceases, and next thing you know, now you're feeling unpleasant feeling, for whatever reason, when you become self-aware of it, you find it as already there, being felt, and you're within it.

66
00:06:39,783 --> 00:06:47,485
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there is no point in between one feeling, that then passes into next feeling, that then passes into next feeling, that then passes into next feeling.

67
00:06:47,545 --> 00:06:55,028
[SPEAKER_01]: Because that point will require you to step outside of your experience as a whole, and observe that change from one, to two, to three.

68
00:06:55,048 --> 00:06:55,868
[SPEAKER_01]: But you are within it.

69
00:06:56,701 --> 00:07:01,305
[SPEAKER_01]: So, all you have is the enclosure of this kind, of this color, of this feeling.

70
00:07:02,145 --> 00:07:09,451
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, within that, you're thinking, planning, acting, forgetting, greed, aversion, delusion, or sense restraint, virtue, all that.

71
00:07:10,412 --> 00:07:13,975
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, oh, now I find myself within another feeling.

72
00:07:14,235 --> 00:07:15,236
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, how did that happen?

73
00:07:15,656 --> 00:07:17,538
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, that becomes irrelevant question.

74
00:07:18,824 --> 00:07:19,785
[SPEAKER_01]: It matters to somebody.

75
00:07:19,865 --> 00:07:21,826
[SPEAKER_01]: How did feeling change from one to the other?

76
00:07:21,906 --> 00:07:23,627
[SPEAKER_01]: Can I observe the moment in between?

77
00:07:24,447 --> 00:07:36,835
[SPEAKER_01]: A person who would be asking those questions is the person that refuses to give up the view, or is unable to give up the view, because he's not aware of it, of the external sense of self that observes this and that wants to monitor this change.

78
00:07:37,255 --> 00:07:40,136
[SPEAKER_03]: Which is what, like, sensuality, ill will...

79
00:07:40,176 --> 00:07:41,037
[SPEAKER_03]: Exactly.

80
00:07:41,237 --> 00:07:44,598
[SPEAKER_01]: All of these unwholesome states rely on that perversion of that same order.

81
00:07:45,039 --> 00:07:59,685
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the point here is then to recognize that, okay, so, I might really feel that it's important to find an answer how this feeling abruptly, now I feel this abruptly, now I feel neutral feeling abruptly, now it's pleasure abruptly, and so on.

82
00:08:00,025 --> 00:08:01,906
[SPEAKER_01]: How does that change from one to the other?

83
00:08:02,426 --> 00:08:03,007
[SPEAKER_01]: The pressure

84
00:08:03,607 --> 00:08:10,873
[SPEAKER_01]: For that question, you need to basically subdue, and not waste your time trying to answer, because you're going to fall into speculative view.

85
00:08:11,233 --> 00:08:11,774
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, again...

86
00:08:13,114 --> 00:08:26,964
[SPEAKER_01]: If you're very careful and transparent, you realize it's un... you'll be unable... you cannot possibly think outside of yourself, from which point you will have a neutral reference that tells you how one feeling for you, while it's being felt, becomes another.

87
00:08:27,745 --> 00:08:34,950
[SPEAKER_01]: So you realize any notion of answering this requires the notion of that external world independent of my five aggregates, and that's fundamental wrong view.

88
00:08:36,581 --> 00:08:49,895
[SPEAKER_01]: So, instead of then trying to answer it, or trying to observe it through a meditation technique, like to narrow down the moments, it doesn't matter how closely you observe one moment to the next moment, the change between one to the next is always abrupt.

89
00:08:51,096 --> 00:08:52,057
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not something you can see.

90
00:08:52,097 --> 00:08:56,902
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if you were to see the change between moment A to moment B, well, there would be another moment.

91
00:08:57,951 --> 00:09:02,820
[SPEAKER_01]: In other words, anything that you can observe is within that experience that already endures.

92
00:09:02,880 --> 00:09:09,493
[SPEAKER_01]: It's within that feeling, it's within that five aggregates, basically, that cannot be stepped outside of.

93
00:09:12,052 --> 00:09:14,293
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's the practical point of that sutta.

94
00:09:14,313 --> 00:09:21,814
[SPEAKER_01]: It's exactly to recognize that it doesn't matter how specific the moment I'm observing might be.

95
00:09:21,854 --> 00:09:32,917
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't matter how, you know, pleasing and elaborate and satisfactory my explanation of the external process of change or flux can be.

96
00:09:33,537 --> 00:09:38,978
[SPEAKER_01]: Fundamentally, all of that is secondary to the presently enduring feeling, whichever that feeling is.

97
00:09:40,507 --> 00:09:41,387
[SPEAKER_01]: So, for as long...

98
00:09:41,427 --> 00:09:43,888
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's not about changing that feeling.

99
00:09:43,968 --> 00:09:47,010
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not about seeing how it changes from externally.

100
00:09:47,110 --> 00:09:49,971
[SPEAKER_01]: It's about not putting it second while it lasts.

101
00:09:51,492 --> 00:10:00,956
[SPEAKER_01]: So that he knows that in the current container of the experience as a whole, whereby a neutral feeling is currently present, that's the only feeling felt there.

102
00:10:02,096 --> 00:10:03,757
[SPEAKER_01]: Everything else is second to it.

103
00:10:04,992 --> 00:10:07,374
[SPEAKER_01]: And maintain that order, and then what then?

104
00:10:07,455 --> 00:10:08,175
[SPEAKER_01]: What's next thing?

105
00:10:08,235 --> 00:10:12,760
[SPEAKER_01]: What, what, what... Well, next thing is, when you exactly ask that question, what do I do next?

106
00:10:12,800 --> 00:10:15,202
[SPEAKER_01]: You see, oh, is there another feeling?

107
00:10:15,343 --> 00:10:16,904
[SPEAKER_01]: Or it's still the same feeling that's present?

108
00:10:17,705 --> 00:10:23,271
[SPEAKER_01]: If it's still the same feeling, you include that question as second to that presently enduring feeling, and thus you don't lose the right order.

109
00:10:23,931 --> 00:10:26,434
[SPEAKER_01]: But, if you then find out yourself, oh, this is...

110
00:10:26,534 --> 00:10:27,435
[SPEAKER_01]: I feel unpleasant now.

111
00:10:29,073 --> 00:10:34,955
[SPEAKER_01]: Instead of how did it come to be, and psychologists about it, you start recognizing, okay, that's the only feeling felt.

112
00:10:35,455 --> 00:10:43,298
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, but that past feeling that I remember, it's now the memory, the perception, within this presently enduring unpleasant feeling.

113
00:10:44,179 --> 00:10:49,420
[SPEAKER_01]: So there is no one container as a whole morphing into next one.

114
00:10:49,520 --> 00:10:50,441
[SPEAKER_01]: All you have is one

115
00:10:51,535 --> 00:10:53,776
[SPEAKER_01]: One, one, one.

116
00:10:54,596 --> 00:10:58,457
[SPEAKER_01]: In other words, five aggregates, five aggregates, five aggregates.

117
00:10:58,797 --> 00:11:03,619
[SPEAKER_01]: Or, in another words, as the sutra described, five aggregates are fading in, five aggregates fading away.

118
00:11:03,939 --> 00:11:05,219
[SPEAKER_01]: Fading in, fading away.

119
00:11:05,319 --> 00:11:05,959
[SPEAKER_01]: That's all you have.

120
00:11:06,760 --> 00:11:12,261
[SPEAKER_01]: Coming and going, rising and falling, whichever way you describe it, on the level of the experience as a whole.

121
00:11:13,442 --> 00:11:17,183
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why, like Buddha Vipassana, Digha Nikaya, he contemplated that.

122
00:11:17,723 --> 00:11:20,724
[SPEAKER_01]: A rising and ceasing, rising and falling of the five aggregates.

123
00:11:21,822 --> 00:11:26,204
[SPEAKER_01]: For the complete liberation, for the complete arahantship and becoming sama-sambuddha.

124
00:11:27,964 --> 00:11:51,172
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if you contemplate every single arisen experience as a whole, as a container in itself, that endures for as long as it wants to endure, so to speak, and any notion of sense of self, I am, conceit, present, future, loves, fears, worries, anything, any passion, greed, aversion, distraction, any hindrance you might have, you put that second within this presently enduring container,

125
00:11:52,210 --> 00:11:53,511
[SPEAKER_01]: You do not pervert the order.

126
00:11:54,191 --> 00:11:57,633
[SPEAKER_01]: Basically, the only possible result of that is dispassion.

127
00:11:58,633 --> 00:11:59,053
[SPEAKER_00]: Nothing else.

128
00:12:00,074 --> 00:12:02,535
[SPEAKER_01]: And, in the nutshell, that's exactly the practice of satipaṭṭhāna.

129
00:12:03,738 --> 00:12:21,811
[SPEAKER_01]: So, this sutta list mentions the three feelings as the point, but you realize you could practice exactly the same principle on the level of the body posture, or simply on the level of the body being there as a necessary container for any past, present, future memories, hindrances, and so on.

130
00:12:23,032 --> 00:12:27,054
[SPEAKER_01]: Feeling perceptions, in the sense of states of mind.

131
00:12:27,294 --> 00:12:28,355
[SPEAKER_01]: You perceive your states of mind.

132
00:12:28,595 --> 00:12:29,355
[SPEAKER_01]: What is my mood?

133
00:12:29,415 --> 00:12:30,476
[SPEAKER_01]: What is my general mood?

134
00:12:30,536 --> 00:12:31,577
[SPEAKER_01]: Is it elated?

135
00:12:31,877 --> 00:12:32,437
[SPEAKER_01]: Depressed?

136
00:12:32,817 --> 00:12:40,061
[SPEAKER_01]: So, instead of thinking like you are this entity that goes through these different moods, you recognize it's... No.

137
00:12:40,461 --> 00:12:46,844
[SPEAKER_01]: These different moods keep containing this entity that I keep confusing it to be the same person, the same

138
00:12:48,302 --> 00:12:51,803
[SPEAKER_01]: The same phenomenon that exists now, independent of these moods.

139
00:12:52,303 --> 00:12:53,063
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's impossible.

140
00:12:53,363 --> 00:12:55,724
[SPEAKER_01]: Or dhammas, just in general.

141
00:12:56,004 --> 00:12:57,944
[SPEAKER_01]: The four satipaṭṭhāna is just the dhammas.

142
00:12:58,324 --> 00:13:03,485
[SPEAKER_01]: The actual phenomena, in that most precise phenomenological sense.

143
00:13:04,485 --> 00:13:12,347
[SPEAKER_01]: Every presence of every thought, on that phenomenological basis, you realize that, well, that's a container in and of itself, for this whole experience.

144
00:13:14,688 --> 00:13:15,628
[SPEAKER_01]: It's what comes first.

145
00:13:15,908 --> 00:13:16,668
[SPEAKER_01]: It's what endures.

146
00:13:17,205 --> 00:13:18,106
[SPEAKER_03]: Not the continuity.

147
00:13:18,246 --> 00:13:19,147
[SPEAKER_03]: The sense of continuity...

148
00:13:19,167 --> 00:13:20,248
[SPEAKER_01]: Sense of continuity is second.

149
00:13:20,328 --> 00:13:26,734
[SPEAKER_01]: And once you put it second, well, it ceases to be that continuous thing that exists outside of your sense of... of your experience as a whole.

150
00:13:27,875 --> 00:13:28,376
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't...

151
00:13:29,551 --> 00:13:31,373
[SPEAKER_03]: Choose not to have the sense of continuity.

152
00:13:31,413 --> 00:13:32,634
[SPEAKER_03]: This is the only way to uproot it.

153
00:13:32,654 --> 00:13:33,034
[SPEAKER_03]: Exactly.

154
00:13:33,134 --> 00:13:33,955
[SPEAKER_03]: Is to change the order.

155
00:13:33,975 --> 00:13:34,075
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

156
00:13:34,275 --> 00:13:37,318
[SPEAKER_03]: To say, like, I'm refusing to have this sense of continuity.

157
00:13:37,378 --> 00:13:37,798
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

158
00:13:37,899 --> 00:13:43,183
[SPEAKER_01]: And that sense of continuity, basically, is what it's kind of... would kind of remain to some extent.

159
00:13:44,084 --> 00:13:48,908
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when complete dispassion is developed, in the case of an arahant, that sense of continuity

160
00:13:49,729 --> 00:14:13,847
[SPEAKER_01]: This is what's called pūgala, what's called individual, what's called basically the history of these five aggregates, the habits, the ways it was operating, that are now freed from greed, aversion, delusion, freed from these influxes of asavas and pollutions, but to some extent they remain standing there for as long as the five aggregates don't break apart.

161
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:24,766
[SPEAKER_01]: So that sense of continuity will not be confused for the sense of self, independent of the feeling, of the perception, of the mood, of the dhammas, of the body.

162
00:14:25,766 --> 00:14:31,090
[SPEAKER_01]: It will simply be, yeah, it's the same five aggregates that have been enduring for this long.

163
00:14:31,877 --> 00:14:36,320
[SPEAKER_03]: That's the non-persisting, world-changing in the Anguttara 347.

164
00:14:36,360 --> 00:14:36,980
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

165
00:14:37,140 --> 00:14:46,066
[SPEAKER_03]: It's, it's, yeah, but obviously it's impossible as a non-Arahant to, to like, yeah, imagine or conceive that, but it's... You can't.

166
00:14:46,086 --> 00:14:48,167
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, if you're conceiving it, that's already a mistake.

167
00:14:48,187 --> 00:14:48,728
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, obviously, yeah.

168
00:14:48,828 --> 00:14:49,748
[SPEAKER_01]: It's going to be conceiving.

169
00:14:49,929 --> 00:14:50,149
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

170
00:14:50,789 --> 00:15:07,021
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the only way is to... as I said, you won't provide, or you can try, but... and you can provide an answer, but it will never be accurate, because providing an answer requires that external point of view to what's happening here and now, moment to moment to moment.

171
00:15:07,201 --> 00:15:11,404
[SPEAKER_01]: And doesn't matter how hard you concentrate within moment to moment, you're still doing it internally.

172
00:15:11,444 --> 00:15:13,105
[SPEAKER_01]: You're still doing it as...

173
00:15:15,299 --> 00:15:18,243
[SPEAKER_01]: As someone who is fully enclosed by each moment.

174
00:15:18,763 --> 00:15:23,909
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it doesn't matter how many moments you observed, you're equally enclosed within each and every one of them.

175
00:15:25,131 --> 00:15:25,451
[SPEAKER_01]: That's it.

176
00:15:25,551 --> 00:15:26,252
[SPEAKER_01]: Every single time.

177
00:15:27,393 --> 00:15:31,438
[SPEAKER_01]: And the more you narrow in between the moments, well, that's another moment you're enclosed with.

178
00:15:32,550 --> 00:15:42,837
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there is no way out through that concentrating techniques or obviously through like a speculative mystical experiences that take you outside of yourself.

179
00:15:42,878 --> 00:15:43,478
[SPEAKER_01]: It's impossible.

180
00:15:43,518 --> 00:15:47,281
[SPEAKER_01]: Everything you experience is on the basis of your experience.

181
00:15:47,301 --> 00:15:52,404
[SPEAKER_01]: Doesn't matter if it's unfamiliar, if it's unknown, it's still experience real as such.

182
00:15:53,323 --> 00:16:03,915
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the recognition is then, is to discern rightly, with the right view, these correctly enduring reference points, body, feeling, moods, states of mind.

183
00:16:05,527 --> 00:16:12,793
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's when you recognize that you don't get rid of the feeling, you don't get rid of the state of mind, you just see it for what it is to the extent that it is.

184
00:16:12,893 --> 00:16:14,695
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's exactly what satipaṭṭhāna describes.

185
00:16:15,215 --> 00:16:18,298
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, he knows elated mind as elated mind.

186
00:16:18,498 --> 00:16:18,938
[SPEAKER_01]: That's it.

187
00:16:18,958 --> 00:16:22,021
[SPEAKER_01]: To the extent it... the mind is as such, he knows it as such.

188
00:16:22,381 --> 00:16:24,282
[SPEAKER_01]: He knows depressed mind as depressed mind.

189
00:16:25,023 --> 00:16:26,204
[SPEAKER_01]: He knows it.

190
00:16:26,244 --> 00:16:30,427
[SPEAKER_01]: He does not observe it or tries to psychologize it or find a way out of it.

191
00:16:30,487 --> 00:16:33,369
[SPEAKER_01]: He simply knows it and that means he puts it in the right place.

192
00:16:34,230 --> 00:16:42,356
[SPEAKER_01]: He knows it as first and everything else, every pressure, any other hindrance they might want to make you doubt it, change it, do this, do that.

193
00:16:43,256 --> 00:16:48,460
[SPEAKER_01]: He puts that second within the enduring state of mind or within the enduring state of feeling.

194
00:16:49,481 --> 00:16:50,582
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the contemplation.

195
00:16:55,446 --> 00:17:08,432
[SPEAKER_00]: So you could say the the essential difference is basically instead of seeing things or trying to see feeling as a thing that you can act towards or against,

196
00:17:09,570 --> 00:17:13,832
[SPEAKER_00]: It's basically, like you said, to see it as being there beforehand.

197
00:17:14,353 --> 00:17:14,953
[SPEAKER_00]: Before you even...

198
00:17:14,973 --> 00:17:15,573
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

199
00:17:15,693 --> 00:17:16,033
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

200
00:17:16,073 --> 00:17:18,255
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's... Before you can even act towards it, or against it.

201
00:17:18,395 --> 00:17:19,335
[SPEAKER_00]: That's a point also.

202
00:17:19,355 --> 00:17:22,117
[SPEAKER_01]: You might not be clear on the basis of what I said, but that's... yeah.

203
00:17:22,437 --> 00:17:37,825
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when you find yourself already feeling such and such feeling, that's... that's like... the key is to recognize there was no, like, first moment from which you saw that feeling start, because that implies you were there before the feeling, outside of the feeling.

204
00:17:38,508 --> 00:17:38,648
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

205
00:17:38,848 --> 00:17:48,836
[SPEAKER_01]: You already find, whether it's the body posture, whether it's the feeling, whether it's the state of mind, mood, whether it's the dhammas, you find them as already there, given beforehand.

206
00:17:48,856 --> 00:17:49,637
[SPEAKER_01]: They're already there.

207
00:17:49,657 --> 00:17:50,278
[SPEAKER_01]: You've found them.

208
00:17:50,378 --> 00:17:51,178
[SPEAKER_01]: You recollected them.

209
00:17:51,218 --> 00:17:51,859
[SPEAKER_01]: You brought them up.

210
00:17:51,999 --> 00:17:52,559
[SPEAKER_01]: But they were there.

211
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:54,301
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's that recognition.

212
00:17:54,461 --> 00:17:54,561
[SPEAKER_01]: Ah!

213
00:17:54,881 --> 00:17:56,423
[SPEAKER_01]: So, they did not originate from you.

214
00:17:57,738 --> 00:17:58,779
[SPEAKER_01]: You're not their creator.

215
00:17:59,179 --> 00:18:03,324
[SPEAKER_01]: You find them, and then you act out of them, and by doing so, you appropriate them.

216
00:18:03,424 --> 00:18:10,333
[SPEAKER_01]: You put yourself first, and by putting yourself first, you become the owner of these things, even pains and bad moods that you don't want.

217
00:18:10,953 --> 00:18:11,794
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why people like...

218
00:18:12,761 --> 00:18:17,386
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't help but feel affected by the bad mood, the bad feeling.

219
00:18:17,466 --> 00:18:20,369
[SPEAKER_01]: Can't help but take it as yours, their own mind.

220
00:18:20,409 --> 00:18:22,631
[SPEAKER_01]: They can't just say, oh, I won't take it as mine.

221
00:18:22,671 --> 00:18:22,891
[SPEAKER_01]: Why?

222
00:18:22,971 --> 00:18:25,293
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, because on other occasions, they keep taking it as mine.

223
00:18:25,634 --> 00:18:27,696
[SPEAKER_01]: Through perverting their road, that's all it takes.

224
00:18:28,725 --> 00:18:32,187
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you would... you would not be observing that feeling, how it lasts.

225
00:18:32,387 --> 00:18:52,060
[SPEAKER_01]: You would simply find it there, know it as an enduring container, and your sense of self, that's... used to be regarded as the owner, as the one who acts, who sorts the feelings out, who... who manages them, this... all of that, you first restrain, in order to place it second within the enduring container of the feeling.

226
00:18:52,961 --> 00:18:53,781
[SPEAKER_01]: For how long you do it?

227
00:18:53,801 --> 00:18:56,383
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, for as long as that feeling... for until that feeling changes.

228
00:18:57,213 --> 00:19:00,594
[SPEAKER_01]: And that feeling changes, then you find yourself feeling another feeling, as the Sutta says.

229
00:19:01,314 --> 00:19:03,375
[SPEAKER_01]: All you can feel is one feeling at the time.

230
00:19:04,135 --> 00:19:04,795
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what do you do then?

231
00:19:04,855 --> 00:19:05,615
[SPEAKER_01]: You do the same thing.

232
00:19:06,436 --> 00:19:17,259
[SPEAKER_01]: So, obviously, in... if it's the pleasant feeling that you're enduring, the leaning that you would have to be restraining and containing would be to prolong that pleasure to get more of it.

233
00:19:17,539 --> 00:19:21,840
[SPEAKER_01]: If it's unpleasant feeling that you're enduring, the leaning that you would have to be restraining,

234
00:19:23,923 --> 00:19:28,466
[SPEAKER_01]: The leaning that you would have to be restraining is aversion towards it, to get rid of it.

235
00:19:29,387 --> 00:19:43,077
[SPEAKER_01]: And if it's a neutral feeling that you're currently enclosed within, well, what you have to restrain is basically indolence, distraction, boredom, delusion.

236
00:19:43,417 --> 00:19:48,741
[SPEAKER_01]: Not knowing that feeling for what it is, that neutrality, on account of what's being felt.

237
00:19:53,113 --> 00:20:01,421
[SPEAKER_03]: Could you describe those as, like, craving, aversion, distraction, as, like, trying to employ continuity, in a way?

238
00:20:01,722 --> 00:20:02,602
[SPEAKER_03]: Trying to... Yeah.

239
00:20:02,663 --> 00:20:04,324
[SPEAKER_01]: Continuity will pressure you, basically.

240
00:20:04,705 --> 00:20:05,666
[SPEAKER_01]: Again, not continuity.

241
00:20:06,106 --> 00:20:16,857
[SPEAKER_01]: The sense of ownership, the sense of self, the sense of craving, the habit of putting yourself first, the weight of that will pressure you, will want to maintain itself.

242
00:20:17,895 --> 00:20:19,636
[SPEAKER_01]: The momentum of it.

243
00:20:19,916 --> 00:20:24,858
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's kind of the... what you need to kind of work against.

244
00:20:26,339 --> 00:20:33,162
[SPEAKER_01]: And when that weight disappears, then it becomes inconceivable to actually change the order, because you realize the order was never changed.

245
00:20:33,402 --> 00:20:36,083
[SPEAKER_01]: Impermanence was always impermanence.

246
00:20:36,303 --> 00:20:37,463
[SPEAKER_01]: Anatta was always anatta.

247
00:20:37,664 --> 00:20:38,644
[SPEAKER_01]: Unownership was always...

248
00:20:38,764 --> 00:20:40,445
[SPEAKER_01]: Things that are unownable, they were unownable.

249
00:20:40,805 --> 00:20:43,026
[SPEAKER_01]: It was just you being completely deluded in regard to it.

250
00:20:43,671 --> 00:20:51,255
[SPEAKER_03]: So, basically, employ continuity means cover up the factual discontinuity that is unavoidable.

251
00:20:51,375 --> 00:20:51,876
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, yeah.

252
00:20:51,916 --> 00:20:58,820
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, as I said initially, that the weight on that... on the sense of self being put first...

253
00:21:00,291 --> 00:21:06,777
[SPEAKER_01]: That will pressure you, basically, to maintain it there, because it's going to feel unpleasantly, if you start shifting that weight away from it.

254
00:21:07,357 --> 00:21:16,344
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, you know, if sense of self, that's based on the sense of control and ownership, if you start contemplating non-control and non-ownership, well, that sense of self are going to resist.

255
00:21:16,705 --> 00:21:17,585
[SPEAKER_01]: It's going to resist a bit.

256
00:21:17,645 --> 00:21:19,587
[SPEAKER_01]: It's going to... it's not going to take it lightly.

257
00:21:30,778 --> 00:21:47,497
[SPEAKER_02]: In terms of establishing the right order, you get to... maybe you get the idea of what that is, that you are second to the container, you're within experience, confined.

258
00:21:48,970 --> 00:21:55,697
[SPEAKER_02]: And you want to try to keep that vision, you know.

259
00:21:55,977 --> 00:22:01,503
[SPEAKER_02]: So, and the only way to see that, okay, sense restraint and so on.

260
00:22:03,757 --> 00:22:17,627
[SPEAKER_02]: It helps to clarify your situation, but Centrist in itself, being aware, being present, momentary, doesn't doesn't give you that right order, that vision, that right vision.

261
00:22:18,408 --> 00:22:22,911
[SPEAKER_01]: So... No, because what you are present, moment to moment, is your perverted order.

262
00:22:23,151 --> 00:22:24,652
[SPEAKER_01]: And you don't know the order.

263
00:22:24,933 --> 00:22:26,073
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't know what comes first.

264
00:22:26,634 --> 00:22:30,457
[SPEAKER_01]: So, practicing moment to moment awareness, or whatever they describe it these days,

265
00:22:31,197 --> 00:22:33,780
[SPEAKER_01]: All you're practicing is moment-to-moment perversion of the order.

266
00:22:34,040 --> 00:22:35,001
[SPEAKER_01]: It remains unchanged.

267
00:22:35,021 --> 00:22:35,181
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

268
00:22:35,201 --> 00:22:39,746
[SPEAKER_01]: Just be mindful of your... Of whatever's there and you don't even know where the problem is.

269
00:22:39,766 --> 00:22:39,966
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

270
00:22:40,847 --> 00:22:51,097
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why body, speech or mind... See, you can get the sense of the right order, like, through pondering, through reflecting and so on,

271
00:22:52,042 --> 00:22:57,526
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you're still perverting it through bodily actions, well, it's not gonna take root.

272
00:22:58,526 --> 00:23:02,729
[SPEAKER_01]: If you're perverting it through verbal actions, it's not gonna grow.

273
00:23:03,389 --> 00:23:05,431
[SPEAKER_01]: And if you're perverting it through mental actions.

274
00:23:05,970 --> 00:23:11,252
[SPEAKER_01]: And perverting it through body, speech or mind, it's exactly acting out of greed, aversion, delusion, conceit, hindrances.

275
00:23:11,272 --> 00:23:24,955
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it takes you away from that, from having perspective or... Well, because they, those, those phenomenon, phenomenon of greed, aversion, desire, sensuality, that is a phenomenon of perverted order.

276
00:23:25,756 --> 00:23:33,618
[SPEAKER_01]: So, choosing to act upon it is equals to choosing to pervert the order, even if you don't necessarily think in those terms.

277
00:23:34,567 --> 00:23:36,871
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why it's unwholesome, just in and of itself.

278
00:23:38,293 --> 00:23:39,795
[SPEAKER_02]: I will control these feelings.

279
00:23:39,855 --> 00:23:40,957
[SPEAKER_02]: I will produce these feelings.

280
00:23:40,977 --> 00:23:44,823
[SPEAKER_01]: Again, you might not even think those thoughts at all, but that's the implication.

281
00:23:44,883 --> 00:23:46,425
[SPEAKER_01]: Basically, put yourself first.

282
00:23:47,567 --> 00:23:52,891
[SPEAKER_01]: So, whenever there is a desire involved, ill-will, distraction, you put yourself first.

283
00:23:52,931 --> 00:23:55,573
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you can contemplate on top of it, the right order, all you want.

284
00:23:55,894 --> 00:24:06,862
[SPEAKER_01]: If your actions are still putting yourself first, in that fundamental existential sense, well, as I said, the right order cannot possibly begin to grow, and everything else that would come from it.

285
00:24:07,703 --> 00:24:16,309
[SPEAKER_02]: So, a person wants to put themselves second, in this right sense, and you have strong feelings of pain.

286
00:24:18,634 --> 00:24:31,018
[SPEAKER_02]: And instead of trying to sort that pain out, you just put it, put yourself... Well, see, first you need to not act out of the pressure to sort the feeling out.

287
00:24:31,779 --> 00:24:34,780
[SPEAKER_01]: That was like you have to, you have to let it endure for what it is.

288
00:24:35,680 --> 00:24:40,922
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's not to say, oh, just endure it blindly like a fool and it will just, wisdom will come out of it.

289
00:24:40,942 --> 00:24:41,682
[SPEAKER_01]: No, of course not.

290
00:24:43,299 --> 00:24:48,768
[SPEAKER_01]: So, first you don't act out of it, it has to endure for what it is, so that you then see your aversion towards it.

291
00:24:50,250 --> 00:24:50,931
[SPEAKER_00]: And put it second.

292
00:24:51,873 --> 00:24:53,295
[SPEAKER_01]: And when you put it second, it's gone.

293
00:24:53,576 --> 00:24:55,639
[SPEAKER_02]: As in, gratuitous unnecessary...

294
00:24:55,978 --> 00:24:56,338
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

295
00:24:56,479 --> 00:25:01,523
[SPEAKER_01]: As in, completely within the arisen feeling that's presently enduring, there is no outside of it.

296
00:25:02,384 --> 00:25:08,290
[SPEAKER_01]: And when you put your aversion second, the pressure to act out of that aversion dissipates, almost instantaneously.

297
00:25:08,490 --> 00:25:16,077
[SPEAKER_01]: When the right order is established, even for a finger snap, as the suttas would say, for that finger snap, the liberation is felt.

298
00:25:17,606 --> 00:25:26,292
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the point there is to then recognize that, okay, out of faith, initially, you don't act out of trying to sort out the unpleasant feeling and so on.

299
00:25:26,833 --> 00:25:28,674
[SPEAKER_01]: You recognize your aversion towards it.

300
00:25:28,774 --> 00:25:35,379
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you basically include the aversion within the pain that endures and not act out of it.

301
00:25:36,380 --> 00:25:39,002
[SPEAKER_01]: And, as I said, the pressure to act out will diminish.

302
00:25:39,820 --> 00:25:40,760
[SPEAKER_01]: If you do it rightly.

303
00:25:41,461 --> 00:25:56,467
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, secondly, then you also get to recognize that that feeling that you found as already being there, arisen on its own, that's why it's going to go away on its own as well, without you needing to act out at all, out of anything.

304
00:25:56,587 --> 00:26:04,951
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the recognition of this manifested feeling becomes the... oh, its manifestation is its unmanifestation.

305
00:26:05,171 --> 00:26:08,152
[SPEAKER_01]: It has to unmanifest because it's manifested.

306
00:26:09,497 --> 00:26:10,478
[SPEAKER_01]: And I don't need to do anything.

307
00:26:10,578 --> 00:26:14,201
[SPEAKER_01]: So, whatever has manifested, that's why it has to unmanifest.

308
00:26:14,381 --> 00:26:16,803
[SPEAKER_01]: Not because it's like this, or like that, or I did this, or I said this.

309
00:26:16,823 --> 00:26:17,123
[SPEAKER_01]: No, no, no.

310
00:26:17,644 --> 00:26:20,486
[SPEAKER_01]: Simply because it is, it will not be.

311
00:26:21,787 --> 00:26:27,171
[SPEAKER_01]: And that, in and of itself, liberates you from anything, everything, the whole saṃsāra, if it's fully developed.

312
00:26:29,994 --> 00:26:30,814
[SPEAKER_01]: Came on its own.

313
00:26:31,835 --> 00:26:32,776
[SPEAKER_01]: Endures on its own.

314
00:26:35,220 --> 00:26:36,361
[SPEAKER_01]: No room for you there.

315
00:26:37,302 --> 00:26:40,304
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the recognition of Sotāpanna, as we mentioned before.

316
00:26:41,625 --> 00:26:45,588
[SPEAKER_01]: Whatever has the nature to manifest, that's why it will unmanifest.

317
00:26:49,431 --> 00:26:51,713
[SPEAKER_01]: So you don't need to wait for quite the opposite.

318
00:26:51,953 --> 00:26:58,078
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't wait for thing to end to see its unmanifestation or to see its impermanence.

319
00:26:58,899 --> 00:27:00,580
[SPEAKER_01]: No, you see it while the thing is there.

320
00:27:03,581 --> 00:27:15,130
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the recognition that manifestation, anything that's manifested in your experience, as a whole, on the level of the five aggregates, because it's manifested, that's why it has to unmanifest.

321
00:27:15,531 --> 00:27:17,392
[SPEAKER_03]: Including the sense of continuity.

322
00:27:17,612 --> 00:27:32,024
[SPEAKER_01]: Including any, any, doesn't matter, far, near, subtle, coarse, broad, general, particular, any phenomenon, to the extent that it's manifested, to the extent that it's present, that, that's why it will unmanifest.

323
00:27:34,060 --> 00:27:34,420
[SPEAKER_00]: That's it.

324
00:27:36,282 --> 00:27:37,163
[SPEAKER_01]: And put that first.

325
00:27:37,883 --> 00:27:38,904
[SPEAKER_01]: Put that container first.

326
00:27:39,905 --> 00:27:40,746
[SPEAKER_01]: And protect it there.

327
00:27:41,206 --> 00:27:42,107
[SPEAKER_01]: Don't violate it.

328
00:27:42,327 --> 00:27:45,409
[SPEAKER_01]: Don't pervert it through your action by body, speech and mind.

329
00:27:47,751 --> 00:27:49,353
[SPEAKER_02]: So, in terms of...

330
00:27:49,393 --> 00:27:58,200
[SPEAKER_02]: So, again, putting yourself second, container first, and trying to keep that right order.

331
00:27:59,842 --> 00:28:06,628
[SPEAKER_02]: Trying to develop it, so that it takes root, or that it... everything flips, flips in the right way.

332
00:28:09,330 --> 00:28:11,052
[SPEAKER_02]: Keep precepts, sense of strength.

333
00:28:12,052 --> 00:28:15,055
[SPEAKER_02]: And then, there's the other exercise of

334
00:28:17,294 --> 00:28:17,814
[SPEAKER_02]: Wakefulness.

335
00:28:18,754 --> 00:28:19,875
[SPEAKER_02]: Continuous wakefulness.

336
00:28:19,975 --> 00:28:21,355
[SPEAKER_02]: Practice of wakefulness.

337
00:28:21,875 --> 00:28:29,357
[SPEAKER_02]: And as I said, you can't be wakeful and present and expect that to sort things out for you.

338
00:28:29,837 --> 00:28:35,639
[SPEAKER_02]: You have to keep awake and present with this right order.

339
00:28:36,299 --> 00:28:36,879
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah.

340
00:28:36,899 --> 00:28:41,060
[SPEAKER_01]: That's where the practice starts with knowing the right order, knowing the right view.

341
00:28:43,445 --> 00:28:47,850
[SPEAKER_01]: If you don't know what the right order is, everything else you do is kind of circumstantial.

342
00:28:47,990 --> 00:28:59,201
[SPEAKER_01]: That's not to say that you shouldn't keep the precepts if you're not a sotāpanna, but it's to say that you should recognize, that you ought to recognize that the practice begins with knowledge of the right order.

343
00:29:00,002 --> 00:29:03,065
[SPEAKER_01]: First is first, second is second, you know, turning the upside down.

344
00:29:05,537 --> 00:29:07,438
[SPEAKER_02]: But anyone can practice wakefulness.

345
00:29:07,839 --> 00:29:08,739
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, exactly.

346
00:29:08,759 --> 00:29:10,020
[SPEAKER_01]: Anybody can do that.

347
00:29:10,641 --> 00:29:16,345
[SPEAKER_01]: But if people do that on the basis of knowing the right order, well, then they are actually progressing.

348
00:29:17,186 --> 00:29:21,329
[SPEAKER_01]: If people keep... anybody can keep the precepts and practice sense restraint.

349
00:29:21,549 --> 00:29:28,894
[SPEAKER_01]: If people do that on the basis of the knowledge of the right order, well, that's pretty much the development of the Noble Eightfold Path.

350
00:29:29,875 --> 00:29:34,739
[SPEAKER_02]: Is it, you know, you maintain wakefulness through the first watch of the night?

351
00:29:36,795 --> 00:29:42,277
[SPEAKER_02]: Through the last watch of the night, so through the day, through the first watch of the night, and in the middle of the night, you go to sleep.

352
00:29:42,837 --> 00:29:44,938
[SPEAKER_02]: You get up and do the same thing.

353
00:29:44,998 --> 00:29:47,679
[SPEAKER_02]: Purify the mind of obstacles.

354
00:29:47,699 --> 00:29:47,939
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

355
00:29:48,019 --> 00:29:48,439
[SPEAKER_02]: To what?

356
00:29:49,079 --> 00:29:49,979
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, what's an obstacle?

357
00:29:50,039 --> 00:29:50,399
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

358
00:29:51,360 --> 00:29:52,140
[SPEAKER_02]: What do you got to know?

359
00:29:52,220 --> 00:29:58,362
[SPEAKER_01]: You have to have... Just randomly, randomly purifying your mind from things you think they shouldn't be there?

360
00:29:59,963 --> 00:30:03,504
[SPEAKER_01]: Or are you purifying the mind from things that are trying to pervert the right order?

361
00:30:04,782 --> 00:30:05,963
[SPEAKER_01]: Are you removing the wrong order?

362
00:30:06,163 --> 00:30:08,264
[SPEAKER_01]: You catch yourself putting yourself first.

363
00:30:08,524 --> 00:30:09,164
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, there you go.

364
00:30:09,304 --> 00:30:10,805
[SPEAKER_01]: That's an impurity.

365
00:30:11,845 --> 00:30:19,269
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you remove that impurity by fixing the right order, by seeing what needs to be seen as first and seeing what needs to be seen as second.

366
00:30:20,609 --> 00:30:25,712
[SPEAKER_02]: So, all those hindrances are things which pervert the order that you're trying to keep.

367
00:30:30,448 --> 00:30:41,757
[SPEAKER_02]: Because you can... yeah, I was reading that, you know, wakefulness, you know, first watch of the night, don't go to sleep for as long as you can, go to sleep in the middle, wake up very early and so on.

368
00:30:43,479 --> 00:30:46,041
[SPEAKER_03]: And if someone takes it... And do it in and of itself, yeah.

369
00:30:46,061 --> 00:30:49,203
[SPEAKER_02]: In and of itself, it can almost drive you mad, because... Yeah.

370
00:30:49,323 --> 00:30:50,584
[SPEAKER_01]: What are you... What are you doing?

371
00:30:50,865 --> 00:30:51,045
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

372
00:30:51,545 --> 00:30:52,486
[SPEAKER_01]: What are you doing it for?

373
00:30:52,666 --> 00:30:52,926
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

374
00:30:54,888 --> 00:30:56,890
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, no, that's really like... the emphasis...

375
00:30:57,735 --> 00:31:03,157
[SPEAKER_01]: The goal should be discernment of the right order, on the basis of virtue and sense restraint.

376
00:31:04,677 --> 00:31:05,417
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the right view.

377
00:31:05,537 --> 00:31:06,418
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the sotāpārtha.

378
00:31:06,458 --> 00:31:08,218
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, you'll know what the practice is.

379
00:31:10,599 --> 00:31:15,461
[SPEAKER_01]: You will then also know how to protect that right order, and other things will fall into place.

380
00:31:16,901 --> 00:31:23,403
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you're just trying to do same, trying to do satipaṭṭhāna, ānāpānasati, that's why I keep saying it applies only to sotāpārthas or higher.

381
00:31:28,127 --> 00:31:33,611
[SPEAKER_01]: You keep trying to do those things, thinking they, in and of itself, will result in this recognition of...

382
00:31:33,711 --> 00:31:34,051
[SPEAKER_01]: It won't.

383
00:31:34,292 --> 00:31:44,660
[SPEAKER_01]: You need to learn what recognitions you have to understand, what anicca is on that right level, and then it has to be endured there until it's kind of seen correctly.

384
00:31:44,700 --> 00:31:54,527
[SPEAKER_01]: You can even listen to this talk, read the suttas, get the sense of the right order and so on, but when, say, unpleasant feeling is present, what do you do?

385
00:31:57,327 --> 00:31:59,488
[SPEAKER_01]: You're craving in aversion to get rid of it.

386
00:32:00,768 --> 00:32:02,429
[SPEAKER_01]: Are you able to contain it?

387
00:32:02,509 --> 00:32:03,869
[SPEAKER_01]: Are you able to put it second?

388
00:32:04,650 --> 00:32:09,391
[SPEAKER_01]: Are you able to then uphold the values of the right order and not act out of it?

389
00:32:10,472 --> 00:32:13,553
[SPEAKER_01]: For months, if it takes that long for that feeling to dissipate.

390
00:32:14,750 --> 00:32:23,039
[SPEAKER_01]: Or, by the end of the day, you have to act out, you have to say something, you have to address this, because it becomes too confining and you can't bear it anymore.

391
00:32:23,619 --> 00:32:24,520
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there you go.

392
00:32:24,560 --> 00:32:30,326
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why there is no right view being developed, because you keep puncturing the container, pretty much.

393
00:32:30,346 --> 00:32:31,668
[SPEAKER_01]: You keep letting the pressure out.

394
00:32:33,383 --> 00:32:38,606
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you can't hold the pressure, well, you need to then build up the container to hold the pressure first.

395
00:32:38,946 --> 00:32:46,709
[SPEAKER_02]: But that's what I think, that's what I think that practice of weightlessness is doing, is maintain... Oh yeah, yeah, that will intensify, yeah.

396
00:32:47,090 --> 00:32:47,850
[SPEAKER_02]: Maintain it.

397
00:32:47,890 --> 00:32:53,513
[SPEAKER_01]: If it's done on the basis of the gradual training, when it comes to do that, you will be able to intensify it like that.

398
00:32:53,593 --> 00:33:00,216
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you just do it as, as I said, as some sort of practice, expecting that it will result in this release, it won't.

399
00:33:00,636 --> 00:33:02,417
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, not of the release that matters, at least.

400
00:33:08,245 --> 00:33:09,306
[SPEAKER_02]: Never distract yourself.

401
00:33:10,387 --> 00:33:11,648
[SPEAKER_02]: Never give in to indolence.

402
00:33:11,708 --> 00:33:13,789
[SPEAKER_02]: Never turn off that...

403
00:33:14,370 --> 00:33:16,511
[SPEAKER_02]: So, even just the fact that you're staying awake.

404
00:33:16,932 --> 00:33:19,874
[SPEAKER_02]: So, if you've got the right order, you've got the idea of it.

405
00:33:19,894 --> 00:33:29,962
[SPEAKER_02]: The fact that you're staying... you've made a determination to stay awake as long as you can, in the face of tiredness and so on, kind of reminds you of your determination.

406
00:33:30,082 --> 00:33:30,722
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, it is.

407
00:33:30,863 --> 00:33:33,905
[SPEAKER_01]: It is, as I said, it is kind of pushing a bit further.

408
00:33:36,394 --> 00:33:45,361
[SPEAKER_01]: Testing it, pressuring the upholding of the right order, so to drain away any impurities that might still be hiding there further, deep inside.

409
00:33:47,583 --> 00:33:56,811
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, because that indolence is that, or that wanting to look away from that pressure.

410
00:33:56,991 --> 00:33:58,452
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, want to distract yourself, yeah.

411
00:33:58,512 --> 00:33:59,193
[SPEAKER_01]: It's very strong.

412
00:33:59,653 --> 00:34:01,815
[SPEAKER_01]: Just forget, forget about it for a bit.

413
00:34:02,255 --> 00:34:03,236
[SPEAKER_01]: Have a break from it.

414
00:34:04,377 --> 00:34:04,778
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

415
00:34:05,972 --> 00:34:15,440
[SPEAKER_01]: Obviously, as I said, somebody in the beginning who doesn't have even the right view or who hasn't like cultivated it sufficiently enough, those things are too subtle to worry about them at that point.

416
00:34:16,481 --> 00:34:18,062
[SPEAKER_01]: First, address the coarse impurities.

417
00:34:18,082 --> 00:34:21,145
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't start the suttas that describe purifying the gold.

418
00:34:21,625 --> 00:34:25,148
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't purify the gold by picking the microscopic bits out, but there's still like

419
00:34:26,754 --> 00:34:29,459
[SPEAKER_01]: lumps of mud, you know, flowing around.

420
00:34:30,240 --> 00:34:33,786
[SPEAKER_01]: No, you get the obvious stuff first out, then the less obvious and so on.

421
00:34:34,306 --> 00:34:38,113
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, when there's nothing else, you get to see, oh, look, no, this is impurity and that.

422
00:34:38,153 --> 00:34:39,154
[SPEAKER_01]: In this, you won't even see it.

423
00:34:39,875 --> 00:34:41,378
[SPEAKER_01]: You're just covered with all the other dirt.

